## 6. Evidence gaps flagged for the Council

- Public MII language in the 2025 Use & Lease for design-manual amendments and passenger-experience capital.
- Financing structure for the incremental $13 B–$15.5 B Dulles scope beyond the $6.99 B IAD CCP already inside the 2025 Use & Lease.
- Measured missed-boarding data from LCY, HEL, and CPH under silence-first policy — none of the airports publishes outcome data suitable for direct benchmarking.
- Employee sound-exposure monitoring history at either IAD or DCA hold rooms.
- Any prior MWAA quiet-terminal or silent-boarding pilot and its measured results.

These are gaps to name in the final deliverable, not gaps to fill with inference.
